1
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:17,540
Drifting on the Nakagawa,
aiming for one certain day,

2
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:24,660
I kick a pebble and my shoes go flying too.

3
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:33,020
Wondering whether you'd save up for me,

4
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:39,140
they laughed that I was still just a kid.

5
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I somehow summon some energy,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
Katsushika, nothing changes,
not even one yawn.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,180
The streetscape is strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,240
From beneath the pointed hat,
from the temizu basin,

9
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:07,460
the evening sun sinks toward
the bowing shrine hall.

10
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:15,920
Why does tomorrow have to end too

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:19,740
Katsushika, Shibamata, happiness too,

12
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:24,700
I've been running wild and only just realized,
I'm such a fool,

13
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:31,340
Full-speed dash! Speedy food stall!

14
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:37,240
Ryōzu! Is Ryōzu here?

15
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:40,740
Senpai said he'd gone out on patrol.

16
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:46,340
Patrol? For him to volunteer for patrol,
that's rather suspicious.

17
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:47,880
Now that you mention it, yes.

18
00:01:50,740 --> 00:01:51,320
Chief.

19
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:56,440
Yes, that Ryotsu apparently borrowed
next month's salary in advance again.

20
00:01:56,440 --> 00:01:57,659
Knowing him,

21
00:01:57,709 --> 00:02:01,200
I suspect he's going to
use it for something no good.

22
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:20,620
Wow, so many food stalls!

23
00:02:21,940 --> 00:02:24,740
Yes, they say it's called Yatai Ginza.

24
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:28,020
During the day it's just an ordinary street,

25
00:02:28,020 --> 00:02:30,800
but when the sun goes down,
the stalls start gathering here.

26
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:34,860
There are all kinds of stalls

27
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:38,060
What's that crowd over there?

28
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:40,900
Come on, come on, step right up!

29
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:43,480
This is the new wave of Yatai Ginza.

30
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:46,780
Ramen, oden, and a beer hall all in one,
the latest model,

31
00:02:46,860 --> 00:02:48,940
the arrival of the three-story food stall!

32
00:02:50,260 --> 00:02:51,820
This looks interesting.

33
00:02:52,020 --> 00:02:53,740
Shall we grab a drink at the beer hall?

34
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:55,120
Well, welcome.

35
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:55,780
Ryo-chan.

36
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:58,500
Nakagawa and Reiko.

37
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:01,620
Senpai,
what are you doing in a place like this?

38
00:03:02,620 --> 00:03:05,710
Well, you should know.
Yatai Ginza is booming right now.

39
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:08,032
So I'm getting into a side business too,

40
00:03:08,082 --> 00:03:10,540
and I've decided to run a food stall.

41
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:13,507
I thought you'd been out of sight lately.

42
00:03:13,557 --> 00:03:15,978
I heard you took an advance on your salary,

43
00:03:16,028 --> 00:03:18,500
and you spent it on this again.

44
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:19,200
Hah,

45
00:03:19,250 --> 00:03:23,175
What I do with my own salary is my business,
isn't it?

46
00:03:23,225 --> 00:03:26,560
If you two aren't customers,
then get lost, get lost.

47
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:28,120
Hey, scram!

48
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:30,080
What is it, Ryotsu?

49
00:03:30,080 --> 00:03:32,660
Two guests for the beer hall!

50
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:35,000
All the way to Sensō-ji, please.

51
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,020
You got dragged into this by Ryo-chan,
didn't you?

52
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:39,580
Hey, shall we stop and have some oden?

53
00:03:39,620 --> 00:03:40,960
Yeah, I'm getting hungry.

54
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:42,800
Thank you! Upstairs, please!

55
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:44,080
Ramen, please.

56
00:03:44,080 --> 00:03:45,080
Welcome!

57
00:03:45,080 --> 00:03:46,300
Yakitori for me.

58
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:48,360
Two for the third-floor beer hall.

59
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:50,800
Once Ryo-chan gets going like this,
nobody can stop him.

60
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:54,620
Honestly, our senior is a real handful.

61
00:03:56,460 --> 00:03:58,040
Here's your beer, thanks for waiting!

62
00:03:58,680 --> 00:04:00,460
Hey, buddy, the yakitori hasn't come yet.

63
00:04:00,460 --> 00:04:02,740
Sorry, I'll bring it out right away.

64
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:09,160
Hey Sagonji, the yakitori's done!

65
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:13,360
Hey Ryo-san, if it's this busy,
my body won't hold out!

66
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:15,220
This is just the beginning!

67
00:04:15,220 --> 00:04:18,400
The showtime is waiting for us from 11 tonight,
so remember that.

68
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:19,880
Showtime?

69
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:22,200
With this many stalls lined up,

70
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:24,580
we have to do something that
makes that kind of impact.

71
00:04:24,580 --> 00:04:27,160
Otherwise we won't
survive here on Yatai Ginza.

72
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:29,620
That's fine,
but who's actually going to do it?

73
00:04:29,920 --> 00:04:31,740
Well, it has to be you, obviously.

74
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:32,520
Me?

75
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:33,080
Yep.

76
00:04:33,460 --> 00:04:35,060
N-no way! You can't be serious!

77
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:36,080
You don't want to?

78
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:37,020
Of course not.

79
00:04:38,380 --> 00:04:39,577
That's a shame.

80
00:04:39,627 --> 00:04:43,680
And I finally got the
new Dokimemo figure, too.

81
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,640
W-what? Really, Ryotsu?

82
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:47,300
Victory!

83
00:04:47,860 --> 00:04:50,245
This new figure is life-size,

84
00:04:50,295 --> 00:04:54,020
with 200 movable joints,
so you can pose it any way you want.

85
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:55,620
Any way I want?

86
00:04:55,620 --> 00:04:57,959
Alright, showtime, no matter what,

87
00:04:58,009 --> 00:05:00,080
whatever it takes, we're doing it!

88
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:02,640
Hey, mister, your yakitori is burning!

89
00:05:02,880 --> 00:05:04,020
Hey, hey, is the oden ready yet?

90
00:05:04,460 --> 00:05:05,300
Better not hit it, or it'll...

91
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:07,440
This one, I'll strike it. Stop dawdling!

92
00:05:08,300 --> 00:05:09,320
Another draft beer.

93
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:10,340
Yes, coming right up!

94
00:05:10,740 --> 00:05:11,240
Here you go, thanks for coming!

95
00:05:11,540 --> 00:05:12,360
The yakitori hasn't come out yet.

96
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:13,680
We'll have it for you right away.

97
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:22,165
Come on, everyone!

98
00:05:22,215 --> 00:05:24,840
It's the show you've all been waiting for!

99
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:28,240
We won't be stingy and say you're
only leaving after seeing Odaiba!

100
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:30,440
Enjoy it to the fullest!

101
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:46,960
Ripped muscle condition!

102
00:05:50,660 --> 00:05:52,220
He's on fire! He's totally ripped!

103
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:57,880
Wow! Wow!

104
00:05:57,880 --> 00:05:58,000
Wow!

105
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:00,480
Amazing!

106
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:03,400
Yeah, go for it!

107
00:06:04,660 --> 00:06:05,060
Incredible!

108
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:11,120
They've totally stolen our customers.

109
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:13,680
We need to put on a show that flashy too.

110
00:06:18,020 --> 00:06:19,960
Hahahahaha!

111
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:21,500
Look, look, look!

112
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:23,880
Just as planned,
we're raking in big profits!

113
00:06:25,620 --> 00:06:27,500
At this rate, you'll wear yourself out.

114
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:30,340
I see. Then how about we have Honda buy it?

115
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:32,660
In exchange, the Dokimemo figure -

116
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:34,520
I'll do it, I'll do it, I'm doing it!

117
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:36,260
Are you motivated now?

118
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:39,840
Then starting tomorrow, we'll be open
during the day as well as at night!

119
00:06:40,860 --> 00:06:41,660
During the day too?

120
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:46,840
That's right. If we get this popular,
tomorrow there'll be stalls copying this one.

121
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:49,500
It's a world of fierce competition,
after all.

122
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:53,500
But daytime oden and a beer hall
won't make any business, right?

123
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:58,980
Exactly! Daytime stalls have to
meet the needs of daytime customers!

124
00:07:02,980 --> 00:07:06,620
It's around noon.
Alright, here should be good enough.

125
00:07:07,980 --> 00:07:10,220
Hey, Sagonji! Here's fine, stop!

126
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:20,340
Hey, Ryotsu. What are you planning to do,
stopping in a place like this?

127
00:07:20,700 --> 00:07:22,600
Now, now, just watch.

128
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:32,640
What is this food stall?

129
00:07:34,260 --> 00:07:35,700
The first floor is a barbershop.

130
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:38,620
You can get a quick trim even
during the busy lunch break.

131
00:07:38,620 --> 00:07:40,520
Behind it is a pachinko parlour.

132
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:42,960
You can blow off steam in a short time.

133
00:07:43,640 --> 00:07:45,700
And on the side, there's mini golf.

134
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:48,800
Practise during lunch and your
score is guaranteed to improve.

135
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:52,420
And even more,
bowling to fight your lack of exercise.

136
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:55,620
And on the second floor,
conveyor belt sushi!

137
00:07:55,670 --> 00:08:00,320
And on top of all that, the third floor is an
all-you-can-eat cake buffet for office ladies!

138
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:04,755
Everything is designed
for busy salarymen and OLs.

139
00:08:04,805 --> 00:08:09,140
Its name says it all: Ryo-chan's food stall,
where everything you need is within reach!

140
00:08:10,540 --> 00:08:13,480
Wow, amazing.
With this, we might actually make it.

141
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:16,658
Attention,
all you salarymen and office ladies!

142
00:08:16,708 --> 00:08:19,805
Come on, come on,
step right up and take a look!

143
00:08:19,855 --> 00:08:22,980
Totally refreshed in
just a short lunch break.

144
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:26,180
A barbershop, pachinko, mini golf, bowling,

145
00:08:26,230 --> 00:08:28,960
and for you office ladies,
all-you-can-eat cake too!

146
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:32,280
Sounds fun. Guess I'll give it a try.

147
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:34,240
All-you-can-eat cake, you say?

148
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:36,120
We'd be crazy not to take
advantage of that, right?

149
00:08:41,060 --> 00:08:43,000
Yes! Just as expected! Woo!

150
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:55,320
Next, anago, please!

151
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:55,960
Argh!

152
00:08:56,580 --> 00:08:59,500
Are we really allowed to
do this without a license?

153
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:02,780
Hey! It's not coming out now!

154
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:05,680
Hey! Extra meter at the station!

155
00:09:06,640 --> 00:09:08,920
Hey! Ryotsu! Take over for a bit!

156
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:10,280
Coming right up!

157
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:28,200
We're raking it in, we're raking it in!

158
00:09:28,700 --> 00:09:31,720
But at this rate, no matter how many
bodies you have, it won't be enough.

159
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:34,320
Exactly, at this rate we
still don't have enough stalls.

160
00:09:34,320 --> 00:09:36,180
Are you still planning to add more?

161
00:09:40,860 --> 00:09:43,220
You're going to patrol Yatai Ginza?

162
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:46,540
Since the number of stalls
has suddenly increased lately,

163
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:49,400
if trouble breaks out over customers,
it'll be bad news.

164
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:50,820
Then I'm leaving the rest to you.

165
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:52,440
Chief.

166
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:56,900
What should we do? If it turns out
the source of the trouble is Senpai...

167
00:09:56,900 --> 00:09:59,160
But, well, it's the usual thing, so...

168
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:05,281
Just as I thought,

169
00:10:05,331 --> 00:10:08,800
and sure enough,
someone copied us right away.

170
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:12,000
But we're finally one step ahead of them.

171
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:17,800
Scale!

172
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:20,800
How about that?

173
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:23,620
This is the world's only
seven-storey food stall!

174
00:10:23,620 --> 00:10:26,160
Ramen, oden, yakitori, okonomiyaki,

175
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:28,000
takoyaki, Daiten Sushi,
roasted sweet potatoes.

176
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:31,040
the best menu items picked
by 1,000 office workers,

177
00:10:31,040 --> 00:10:32,500
I'm packing them all in!

178
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:32,820
There you go!

179
00:10:35,680 --> 00:10:36,780
That stall there!

180
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:40,060
Then it's not a stall,
it's the same as a building!

181
00:10:40,060 --> 00:10:41,640
That's an illegal structure!

182
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:42,960
Epujō!

183
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:44,340
Ryotsu!

184
00:10:44,340 --> 00:10:46,880
What do you think you're doing here?

185
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:50,500
That's not true!

186
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:53,280
If you're not Ryotsu, then who is?

187
00:10:53,740 --> 00:10:56,360
No, no! It's a lookalike!

188
00:10:56,740 --> 00:10:58,020
Look, it's Ryotsu!

189
00:10:58,320 --> 00:10:59,100
Stop right there!

190
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:00,900
As if I'd stop!

191
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:06,520
Damn, this is bad! Stop from this side!

192
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:08,280
Easier said than done,
you can't stop on a dime!

193
00:11:15,560 --> 00:11:18,760
Hey, Ryotsu, you idiot!

194
00:11:20,560 --> 00:11:23,940
Yes, Chief, I'm very sorry.

195
00:11:23,940 --> 00:11:25,920
You really are something else.

196
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:28,600
Learn your lesson and never
do anything like that again.

197
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:30,500
Yes, I won't do it again.

198
00:11:30,500 --> 00:11:31,880
You'd better mean it.

199
00:11:31,880 --> 00:11:32,360
Yes.

200
00:11:33,620 --> 00:11:36,960
But this won't stop me
from giving up that easily.

201
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:40,040
I've got a plan.

202
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:50,640
Ramen, oden, yakitori, okonomiyaki,

203
00:11:50,640 --> 00:11:53,060
takoyaki, conveyor-belt sushi,
even roasted sweet potatoes.

204
00:11:53,060 --> 00:11:55,400
Catering to every need, it's called

205
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:59,400
Ryo-chan's Yatai Train
Heavyweight Special Edition!

206
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:02,320
And with computers installed,

207
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:05,720
you can buy concert tickets
or pay your electric bill too.

208
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:07,880
And on top of that,
for souvenirs for your family,

209
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:13,860
one after another,
who else would go this far?

210
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:17,280
Winning the competition takes this much, obviously.
I'll use any means necessary.

211
00:12:17,400 --> 00:12:19,220
I'm going all out.

212
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:21,840
Here's your ramen, sir.

213
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:26,100
Hey, bud, can you deliver some oden?

214
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:26,980
Of course.

215
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:29,540
Hey, Sakonji, I need an oden delivery.

216
00:12:29,940 --> 00:12:30,300
What?

217
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:32,100
Hey, another beer over here.

218
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:32,700
Coming right up.

219
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:34,560
Hey, add some yakitori to my order.

220
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:35,040
Sure.

221
00:12:35,180 --> 00:12:35,760
Where's the yakitori?

222
00:12:36,140 --> 00:12:37,200
I'll bring it right out.

223
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:52,360
That one...

224
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:54,260
Boss, what is it, sir?

225
00:12:54,890 --> 00:12:57,440
It looks like a food stall,
but they're doing pretty well.

226
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:02,380
There's still time before
the joint drill out at sea.

227
00:13:02,380 --> 00:13:04,200
Let's grab a bite to eat.

228
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:06,840
Leave Number 2 behind and
land all other aircraft.

229
00:13:09,380 --> 00:13:10,920
Hey, Sakonji, your change is late.

230
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:11,820
Here you go.

231
00:13:12,780 --> 00:13:14,300
This music?

232
00:13:19,820 --> 00:13:22,000
Sure enough, it's Colonel Bagryu's "Apache."

233
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:24,020
Why would it be here of all places?

234
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:28,260
Hey,

235
00:13:28,310 --> 00:13:32,860
Leave your money!

236
00:13:33,460 --> 00:13:34,360
Damn it!

237
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:43,120
Yeah, that old man Bakuryu...

238
00:13:43,120 --> 00:13:45,700
Getting in the way of
other people's business!

239
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:24,660
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah...

240
00:14:24,660 --> 00:14:27,220
My men and I are going to
take over the whole place!

241
00:14:27,220 --> 00:14:28,720
Serve everyone!

242
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:29,300
Good morning.

243
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:36,700
Let's get the eating and drinking started!

244
00:14:44,340 --> 00:14:48,080
I'll have the beef tongue
and liver yakitori, salted.

245
00:14:50,940 --> 00:14:53,200
We can't do business with these guys around.

246
00:14:54,660 --> 00:14:59,000
Let's send them home.
Plenty of customers came in, didn't they?

247
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,340
Ryo-san, you're so thoughtful!

248
00:15:03,020 --> 00:15:03,340
Aaaaaah...

249
00:15:03,340 --> 00:15:11,960
It soaks right into my very soul!
Come on, let's have another round!

250
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:21,340
Waiting on the yakitori

251
00:15:25,220 --> 00:15:26,940
Not enough grilling!

252
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:29,480
Attack helicopter No. 2

253
00:15:29,840 --> 00:15:30,200
Yes!

254
00:15:30,880 --> 00:15:32,071
Operation 68,

255
00:15:32,121 --> 00:15:34,960
switch to codename Dragon Arrow.

256
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:37,166
Roger, Operation 68,

257
00:15:37,216 --> 00:15:39,700
switching to codename Dragon Arrow.

258
00:15:40,220 --> 00:15:42,480
Hey, Colonel, Dragon Arrow is...

259
00:15:42,480 --> 00:15:44,740
Order up: yakitori, one liver skewer.

260
00:15:44,740 --> 00:15:47,320
Target: yakitori, one liver skewer.

261
00:15:52,740 --> 00:15:54,660
Target lock complete.

262
00:15:54,660 --> 00:15:57,440
Attack start, fire!

263
00:16:02,700 --> 00:16:04,120
Yeah, direct hit!

264
00:16:04,650 --> 00:16:08,300
What a fuss over a single yakitori skewer!

265
00:16:10,300 --> 00:16:12,860
Alright, now let's get some oden.

266
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:17,160
Deusuji, give me some potatoes.

267
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:18,980
The potatoes are still hard!

268
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:22,400
What? Do you think you
can get away with that?

269
00:16:22,740 --> 00:16:24,580
Let's prepare a flamethrower.

270
00:16:24,580 --> 00:16:25,780
A flamethrower?

271
00:16:26,220 --> 00:16:26,680
Here we go.

272
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:35,800
Finished.

273
00:16:36,540 --> 00:16:37,680
Operation successful.

274
00:16:38,280 --> 00:16:40,220
Are we just going to
leave him like this, Ryotsu?

275
00:16:40,220 --> 00:16:43,820
Anyway, we need to get him dead drunk and
onto the helicopter as fast as possible.

276
00:16:43,820 --> 00:16:44,560
R-right, okay.

277
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:45,600
Mm.

278
00:16:47,180 --> 00:16:49,160
Come on, Colonel, let's keep going!

279
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:59,300
Haah, haah, haah.

280
00:17:00,460 --> 00:17:03,221
Hey, squid have ten legs,

281
00:17:03,271 --> 00:17:05,520
so why do octopuses have eight?

282
00:17:07,660 --> 00:17:11,460
There's an octopus den,
so why isn't there a squid den?

283
00:17:11,600 --> 00:17:13,800
Come on, come on, drink more, go on!

284
00:17:14,340 --> 00:17:14,860
Here you go!

285
00:17:18,540 --> 00:17:20,855
Baki-chan, what a great drinking pace.

286
00:17:20,905 --> 00:17:22,680
Come on, another one. Here, another.

287
00:17:28,200 --> 00:17:29,480
I feel great.

288
00:17:32,080 --> 00:17:34,000
I know, I'll show you something good.

289
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:37,960
Come on, you should probably just go home already.
You seem pretty drunk.

290
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:39,340
Now, don't say that.

291
00:17:39,940 --> 00:17:44,820
This is the new speed-reactive
bomb our army developed.

292
00:17:44,820 --> 00:17:48,340
It's called
"If you stop, you lose, up-up-up!"

293
00:17:48,340 --> 00:17:51,100
Speed-reactive bomb.

294
00:17:52,680 --> 00:18:01,120
Attach it to something, and the moment the speed drops below 30 km/h, the timer switch flips.
You can even link several of them together.

295
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:06,180
Our body will have everyone
equip them for emergencies. Hey.

296
00:18:06,180 --> 00:18:11,300
We've been training so they
can be set within one minute.

297
00:18:11,680 --> 00:18:12,880
Let's begin!

298
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:20,660
Why do the training here of all places?

299
00:18:21,180 --> 00:18:26,260
If you can't manage it in any situation,
you're not fit for the military.

300
00:18:26,260 --> 00:18:27,100
Set complete.

301
00:18:27,100 --> 00:18:27,980
Set complete.

302
00:18:29,160 --> 00:18:30,040
54 seconds.

303
00:18:30,040 --> 00:18:30,880
Good.

304
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:34,380
What if we set that
thing up and it blows up?

305
00:18:34,380 --> 00:18:35,980
Don't worry.

306
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:38,700
Just press the switch on this remote,

307
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:41,960
and the bomb's timer will stop.

308
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:46,700
D-don't panic.

309
00:18:46,700 --> 00:18:48,500
Under any circumstances,

310
00:18:48,500 --> 00:18:51,600
staying calm and composed is my motto.

311
00:18:52,280 --> 00:18:55,300
Hey, what if it really explodes?

312
00:18:58,060 --> 00:19:01,280
It's about time for the action drill.

313
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:04,780
Everyone, double-time to the helicopter!

314
00:19:04,780 --> 00:19:05,240
Pardon me.

315
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:15,300
Hey, hey, what do we do about the bomb?

316
00:19:15,300 --> 00:19:19,760
Just run! As long as you go over 30 km/h,
it won't explode.

317
00:19:19,760 --> 00:19:21,080
You've got to be joking.

318
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:29,120
As long as you keep running, you'll be fine.
Well, see you later!

319
00:19:30,380 --> 00:19:34,180
I've poured my entire fortune into this stall,
you know!

320
00:19:35,240 --> 00:19:35,700
Hey, let's go!

321
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:36,920
But...

322
00:19:37,720 --> 00:19:41,240
Are you sure? There are Dokyumemo
figures on this stall too!

323
00:19:41,500 --> 00:19:42,300
R-right, that's right!

324
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:53,100
Do something, somehow! Ryo-tsu!

325
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:53,720
Easier said than done!

326
00:19:54,620 --> 00:19:55,360
Damn it!

327
00:19:56,500 --> 00:19:58,700
We'll just give it a try! Don't slow down!

328
00:19:59,220 --> 00:20:00,240
W-what do we do?

329
00:20:00,380 --> 00:20:02,260
Cut the bomb's cord!

330
00:20:02,700 --> 00:20:03,000
Yes!

331
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:03,480
Ryo-tsu!

332
00:20:05,340 --> 00:20:06,020
This one's -

333
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:09,020
How about it, Ryotsu?

334
00:20:09,020 --> 00:20:10,340
Looks like we can manage it?

335
00:20:10,340 --> 00:20:13,300
No good, there are red and blue wires!

336
00:20:13,300 --> 00:20:17,140
With this type of bomb,
if you take it apart wrong, it's boom!

337
00:20:17,140 --> 00:20:18,700
So what do we do?

338
00:20:20,660 --> 00:20:23,520
Ryo, come back! Uphill!

339
00:20:24,020 --> 00:20:24,380
What?

340
00:20:24,380 --> 00:20:26,660
Damn it, hang in there, Kagonji!

341
00:20:26,660 --> 00:20:29,620
No matter what, we can't drop below 30 km/h!

342
00:20:33,260 --> 00:20:37,760
Yay!

343
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:38,560
Come on, Konchi!

344
00:20:43,740 --> 00:20:46,100
The explosions are getting bigger!

345
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:47,780
Never mind that, just run now!

346
00:20:48,560 --> 00:20:50,540
Now it's downhill!

347
00:21:07,740 --> 00:21:09,940
Tamuran, my legs are about to burst!

348
00:21:09,940 --> 00:21:13,460
What are you two doing?

349
00:21:13,460 --> 00:21:15,640
Honda, you came at just the right time.

350
00:21:15,640 --> 00:21:17,410
Hey,

351
00:21:17,460 --> 00:21:21,100
What's the meaning of this?

352
00:21:21,100 --> 00:21:25,120
If it drops below 30 km/h,
this stall explodes.

353
00:21:25,120 --> 00:21:26,380
W-what?

354
00:21:27,380 --> 00:21:29,140
This'll let us catch a little rest.

355
00:21:29,140 --> 00:21:32,480
Got that, Honda?
Don't you dare drop below 30 km/h!

356
00:21:32,860 --> 00:21:35,040
Easier said than done!

357
00:21:38,220 --> 00:21:41,334
What a stunt. How did you keep
running while pulling this thing?

358
00:21:41,384 --> 00:21:42,740
That's not human.

359
00:21:43,060 --> 00:21:44,220
Right, while we have the chance.

360
00:21:45,480 --> 00:21:47,080
W-what are you planning, Ryotsu?

361
00:21:47,420 --> 00:21:51,020
We have to find the remote the Colonel
dropped into the oden pot earlier.

362
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:02,240
What's going on?!

363
00:22:03,580 --> 00:22:05,960
The road's under construction
and the pavement's all peeled up!

364
00:22:06,780 --> 00:22:07,420
What is this!

365
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:12,040
The construction's made the road all bumpy!

366
00:22:19,220 --> 00:22:20,360
Are you all right, Ryotsu?!

367
00:22:21,460 --> 00:22:22,180
What is this?!

368
00:22:24,620 --> 00:22:25,940
We made it!

369
00:22:25,940 --> 00:22:28,380
Aaaaahhh!

370
00:22:28,380 --> 00:22:31,520
Gas-kesu, what?!

371
00:22:31,520 --> 00:22:35,080
Aaaaahhh!

372
00:22:41,500 --> 00:22:45,400
Hahaha.

373
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:51,240
Why do I have to do something like this?!

374
00:22:51,240 --> 00:22:53,020
Yokoisho, yokoisho, yokan!

375
00:22:53,020 --> 00:22:55,900
Koi, koi, koi, yokoi, yokan!

376
00:22:55,900 --> 00:22:58,460
Ugh, senpai, hurry up!

377
00:22:58,460 --> 00:23:00,440
Konnya koso!

378
00:23:00,440 --> 00:23:02,980
Ikkayo!

379
00:23:02,980 --> 00:23:04,120
Yay!

380
00:23:07,580 --> 00:23:08,820
It's hopeless!

381
00:23:08,820 --> 00:23:09,840
Even I can't take this anymore!

382
00:23:11,300 --> 00:23:13,480
It's fine now, if we just press this!

383
00:23:17,400 --> 00:23:18,540
Eeeeeh? We're saved!

384
00:23:25,180 --> 00:23:28,040
Is it already this late?
Time for the regular check-in call

385
00:23:31,020 --> 00:23:39,220
Isn't this the speed-reactive bomb's remote?
Then this thing from before is just a cell phone, damn it!

386
00:23:40,220 --> 00:23:40,580
Aaaaaah!

387
00:23:40,580 --> 00:23:41,700
Aaaaaah!

388
00:23:43,260 --> 00:23:44,720
My vegetables!

389
00:23:44,720 --> 00:23:45,980
Taori!

390
00:23:45,980 --> 00:23:48,480
Why me too?

391
00:23:51,700 --> 00:23:53,800
That drunken old geezer!

392
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:57,060
Next time I see him,
he's not getting off easy!

393
00:24:05,140 --> 00:24:08,160
Transform, transform, another transformation...
you guys!

394
00:24:08,160 --> 00:24:09,960
He's just some cosplay freak!

395
00:24:09,960 --> 00:24:10,960
Stop it!

396
00:24:10,960 --> 00:24:12,940
I'm not dressing up like that!

397
00:24:13,300 --> 00:24:15,300
Why are the people in the
Special Investigation Division

398
00:24:15,300 --> 00:24:17,340
all such perverts?

399
00:24:17,840 --> 00:24:20,560
Next time: Dazzling Transformation,
Moonlight Detective!

400
00:24:20,980 --> 00:24:21,600
See you next time, okay?

401
00:24:38,160 --> 00:24:38,660
Yaaah!

402
00:24:38,760 --> 00:24:39,620
At full speed!

403
00:24:39,620 --> 00:24:40,140
Hurry, hurry!

404
00:24:40,240 --> 00:24:41,020
Don't stop!

405
00:24:41,020 --> 00:24:41,780
Please, please!

406
00:24:41,780 --> 00:24:42,700
Quickly and swiftly!

407
00:24:42,700 --> 00:24:43,280
Waaah!

408
00:24:43,300 --> 00:24:43,960
Terrifying!

409
00:24:44,480 --> 00:24:45,680
Speed up!

410
00:24:46,760 --> 00:24:47,440
Gah! Gah!

411
00:24:47,560 --> 00:24:48,340
Keep steady!

412
00:24:48,340 --> 00:24:49,800
Flash!

413
00:24:49,800 --> 00:24:50,360
Uyaaa!

414
00:24:50,360 --> 00:24:51,300
Bouncing!

415
00:24:51,300 --> 00:24:51,920
Debe debe!

416
00:24:51,940 --> 00:24:52,760
All together!

417
00:24:52,760 --> 00:24:53,320
Roll it up!

418
00:24:53,460 --> 00:24:54,220
Keep moving!

419
00:24:54,220 --> 00:24:56,060
Here they come flying!

420
00:24:56,880 --> 00:24:59,540
Above all, that bomb is amazing -

421
00:25:00,860 --> 00:25:02,940
Everyone, keep going!

422
00:25:04,200 --> 00:25:06,340
If we get here,

423
00:25:09,160 --> 00:25:12,640
look, the last of the energy!

424
00:25:13,940 --> 00:25:17,120
Gaze at tomorrow, believe in yesterday,

425
00:25:17,120 --> 00:25:20,020
paint the universe, and stand on the ground,

426
00:25:20,020 --> 00:25:23,860
Kameari's star spun round in a circle.

427
00:25:26,060 --> 00:25:27,440
This should be fine, right?

428
00:25:27,440 --> 00:25:29,060
Of course it's not fine!

429
00:25:42,400 --> 00:25:43,800
Thank you for watching.

